-- the served source (2026-11-16, Avik: "can't you do all the dev before I set up remote infra"): the
-- hyperactive server holding the source every session shares, HYPERACTIVE_SERVER (ADDRESS:PORT, an
-- IPv4 address), its writes allowed by HYPERACTIVE_TOKEN when the server sets one (lib/server.cub).
-- Each command begins by publishing what an earlier command left unpublished, then taking every
-- change the server has had since the session's last (STORE/source-seq), and ends by publishing the
-- modules it changed; the server takes a module only from the pointer the session had before
-- changing it, else the session takes the server's and the change is written again
h-crlf : List Word
h-crlf = cons #13 (cons #10 nil)
